afe","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"HqPTlLE1mxWyvN4y1stsKA","review_id":"zQyeTmMeY4t88HZgD-up-Q","date":"2018-03-26T22:34:15","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9399462938308716,"text_excerpt":"Oh, how I love this place... I couldn't be more thrilled with the recent pop up of more craft breweries in the NOLA area. Just a short Uber ride from the French Quarter..do yourself a favor and make sure you get to this unique brewery! Though they had many different styles on tap, there was something for everyone AND they were all good. Over all, my favorites were the Caged Canary Grisette and Beeryshnikov En Pointe Baltic Porter (sooooo good!). The space is cute..it was a bit chilly but I'm sure the outside seating is lovely when it's warmer. The staff was knowledgeable and pleasant to talk to. Will definitely return next time I visit!"},{"business_id":"HqPTlLE1mxWyvN4y1stsKA","review_id":"V7pCk5vs0ek_ADBqXdQBDA","date":"2017-06-19T19:29:51","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9376068711280823,"text_excerpt":"It seems like we have gotten to the point where a new brewery opens in New Orleans every month. Trust me, I'm not complaining- I love supporting local beer endeavors. We stopped in here during their grand opening weekend and the place was hopping. I decided to start with their Express Yourself IPA. Hoppy and good, it was everything I like in an IPA, but still light enough to enjoy a few of them. The other beer I really enjoyed was their stout, The Lucy. For a stout, it wasn't heavy at all and while I was wishing that it was a little bit more on the \"rich\" side, I found it quite tasty. David isn't much of a beer drinker, so upon the suggestion of the bartender he got a Rooibos Alt, which i..."},{"business_id":"HqPTlLE1mxWyvN4y1stsKA","review_id":"VC2eYB6J8LTMo_guAAeILg","date":"2017-08-03T19:58:25","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9366192817687988,"text_excerpt":"Seriously loving this place. I visited last week after stopping at 40 Arpent Brewery (just a five minute drive), and I will be back-this weekend! My boyfriend is an assistant brewer at Port Orleans, so we've been hitting up all the local brew joints across the city and meeting the masterminds behind local craft beers. Parleaux definitely gets major points for creativity, sarcasm, aesthetics, and overall atmosphere. This place is great for large groups-there's a bunch of seating outside. On top of the great beer and the chill vibe, they also have food pop ups! I had a sour beer that was made with mango syrup from Hansens Sno-Bliz, and I have to tell you, it was delightful. Fruity, refreshi..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"HqPTlLE1mxWyvN4y1stsKA","photo_id":"UDalWJ_A2EBsrqb_eCmOIA","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/UDalWJ_A2EBsrqb_eCmOIA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8631523847579956},{"business_id":"HqPTlLE1mxWyvN4y1stsKA","photo_id":"XQCFxxFMhxgQj7VNAp6tOw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/XQCFxxFMhxgQj7VNAp6tOw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8017634153366089},{"business_id":"HqPTlLE1mxWyvN4y1stsKA","photo_id":"5oN7tqqvO2WOQ8Fep0KZxg","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/5oN7tqqvO2WOQ8Fep0KZxg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7719608545303345},{"business_id":"HqPTlLE1mxWyvN4y1stsKA","photo_id":"Adc0y8CfSe_flKpUgj3_WA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/Adc0y8CfSe_flKpUgj3_WA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7303386926651001},{"business_id":"HqPTlLE1mxWyvN4y1stsKA","photo_id":"MMBxfSqnDte20A1o2ti9eg","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/MMBxfSqnDte20A1o2ti9eg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7211307883262634}]},"notebook_case":null}
